      "message": "Mentioning this for history purposes:\n\nBionic is newer than what kernel supports.\n\nIt breaks ABI because NL80211_ATTR_MAX_NUM_AKM_SUITES is set to 316, which matches the order number of the enum in bionic but the rest in the middle isn\u0027t available in kernel.\n\nLogcat shows:\n\n```\n07-08 02:24:29.532 11177 11177 E wpa_supplicant: wlan0: nl80211: kernel reports: Attribute failed policy validation\n07-08 02:24:29.533 11177 11177 E wpa_supplicant: wlan0: nl80211: kernel reports: Unsupported attribute\n07-08 02:24:29.533 11177 11177 I wpa_supplicant: wlan0: Association request to the driver failed\n```\n\nBut if you remove 316, then it will be auto-incremented, and userspace will fallback to legacy implementation and wifi still works, but in return you get this spam in logcat:\n\n`Failed to get NL80211_ATTR_MAX_NUM_AKM_SUITES`\n\nBecause NL80211_ATTR_MAX_NUM_AKM_SUITES isn\u0027t matching index anymore.",
